# Self-review audit trail — penpot-rest-ops

## Cycle 1 (fresh reviewer, 2026-06-12)

Verdict: NEEDS-WORK. One IMPORTANT, two IMPROVEMENT.

- IMPORTANT — assets/endpoint-index.md: the index generator unwrapped bare object schemas but not single-element `allOf` wrappers, so 9 commands (create-font-variant, import-binfile, create-team-invitations, create-team-access-request, get-comment-threads, get-font-variants, get-team, get-team-info, get-team-users) showed `req: (none)` while their schemas define fields. None are in the documented priority surface and the resolver (endpoint.py) reads them correctly, but an agent scanning the index for a `(none)` line could POST `{}` and 400 on a hidden required field.
  FIX APPLIED: regenerated the index with an allOf/$ref-aware field extractor (mirrors endpoint.py's resolution); added a header note that `(none)` should be confirmed with the resolver for any non-trivial body. The 9 commands now list their real fields (e.g. create-font-variant → req fontFamily, fontId, fontStyle, fontWeight, teamId).

- IMPROVEMENT — get-team surfaces (index `(none)` vs gotcha `{"id":…}` vs absent from quick-ref). Now reconciled: the spec genuinely marks neither field required, so the index honestly shows `opt: id, fileId`; the gotcha advises passing `{"id": <teamUuid>}` and confirming live. Left as-is (honest across surfaces). Not applied as a doc edit — no inconsistency remains.

- IMPROVEMENT — no live smoke yet (Verified live: None). Expected for an unreviewed forge; the error-envelope shape, transit behavior, and get-team field remain "confirm live" (already flagged in sources.md + gotchas). Deferred to the Phase 2.D smoke (owner's base_url + token).

## Cycle 2 (fresh reviewer, no cycle-1 memory, 2026-06-12)

Verdict: SHIP. Zero Critical, zero Important.

Programmatic field cross-check of all 137 index lines vs the spec's allOf/$ref-resolved schemas: zero mismatches, zero false `req: (none)` (cycle-1 allOf fix holds). Call path + `Authorization: Token` consistent everywhere; uncertain items all flagged "confirm live". All four behavioral flows (create-file, verify-token, list-projects, duplicate-file) walk cleanly; token never leaks; caller-injected credential contract holds exactly (no account resolution / .service-accounts.yaml / scope-walk / .envrc). One non-blocking IMPROVEMENT (resolver prints get-team's mislabeled spec example without a per-command caveat — mitigated by the global "values are noise" header + the gotcha in three places). Not applied (cosmetic).

Loop result: 2 cycles, ending SHIP. forge.status stays `unreviewed` pending human approval.
